 "side": "Dark",
 "description": "The most broken version of musicians I have ever seen!",
 "strategy": "What, were you expecting LIGHT SIDE musicians?  >;)\n\nWhen properly played, this deck can give you a one-shot beatdown of 100+ power, power reduction on your opponent's side of around 20(ish), and up to two characters removed from your opponent's side of the battle (one a la Nizuc Bek, and a possible shot with Nevar Yalnal).\n\nHere's the skinny... between S&V; and Greeata reducing your musicians' deploy cost, and Lyn Me making Fett and Greedo drop for free at the same site, AND the fact that everyone's pullable, you can drop a full-fledged beatdown squad for about 5-6 Force.  You'll have a good shot at stacking your destinies for battle with Tech Mo'r and Omni Box, so you should have no excuse NOT to be able to maximize the beat potential.\n\nFairly straightforward strategy, really.  Drop, beat, use Elis if need be for a second beat, etc.  I'm not going to go in depth on what the musicians do... you guys should know where the cardlists are! (hint: http://www.decipher.com/starwars/cardlists/index.html)\n\nA few card choices:\n\nDefensive Fire - good annoyance card, and also has the possibility of dropping a Houjix from their hand.\n\nLimited Resources - just in case you need something to finish them off.  >;)\n\nNevar Yalnal - as stated above, for additional character removal if needed.  If not... it's a destiny 6 floating in the deck.\n\nJust my little protest deck for the current anti Uh-Oh (V) discussion.  This can be just as devestating, and has just as many ways around it.\n\nEnjoy!\n\nDavid \"Icebreath\" Kangas",
